; prior: Python — `if m.get('missing'):` skips the branch when the key is absent.
; expectation: [get m :missing] yields () ("says nothing"), which is falsy, so
; the else arm runs. The surface reading and the Loon behavior agree.
; principle: Priors are part of the spec (agent-first.md P1) — absence is falsy.
; expect-stdout: absent
[fn main []
  [let m {:a 1}]
  [println [if [get m :missing] "present" "absent"]]]
